      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I think the better solution would be (as you suggested) to try to detect if a player is moving at a very high speed, and if yes, attach the entire quick menu to the player (so they can still move to another world or respawn)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-05-21T17:14:09.777Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The reason why I find this so important is that you can easily get stuck falling infinitely in some worlds or situations. While falling you cannot use the quick menu and click the \"Go Home\" button let alone confirm it. This softlocks you and basically forces you to restart VRChat, which can be disruptive and annoying. Therefor having that option in the action menu, which could also have a confirmation in the action menu as well, would be a good solution for now. Ideally however the quick menu would need to get fixed such that it does not become unusable when the player is moving at high speeds and the confirmation menu should not be in world space, but be attached to the player in some way.",
